  "base_divergences": [
    "parallelism.parseListField: a CRLF block kept only its first item (crlf-block-two-items), a comment line ended a block (comment-line-inside-block), a blank line ended a block silently (depends-interior-blank, writes-blank-and-comment-lines), inline comments stayed in the values, an object entry collapsed to its first line, a key-line comment made the list unreadable, a scalar became null (the CLI then fell to legacy), an unindented list or a comment-only value read as [], and mixed blocks, stray continuations and repeated keys kept the first reading silently.",
    "unit-controller.dependsOf: strict, but a comment line or a key-line comment refused the whole declaration, an inline comment became part of the task ID, and an unindented list (unindented-block) was read as a root, hiding its prerequisite.",
    "must-haves.parseExecutionFields: an unquoted root-qualified first item was misread as an object ({\"primary\": \":src/a.js\"}, the next item dropped), a mixed block dropped its stray line, a continuation after a flow list was ignored, inline comments stayed in the values (a quoted item lost only its opening quote), a flow list with a trailing comment kept the comment and its closing bracket, and a scalar, an empty value or an unindented list was a present non-array. Complete block lists with blank lines were read in full; the U0a-r1 ordinary projection keeps that."
  ],
  "independent_issues": [
    "forge-code-dir.js parseListField is a copy of the pre-343 reader and keeps its divergences (inline comments kept, a comment line ends a block, a leading blank line reads writes as [], a key-line comment makes writes unreadable, object entries collapse to 'root_id: primary', mixed/continuation/repeated forms read leniently). It only feeds the sidecar CODE_DIR/cross-repo attribution, not batch eligibility, so it is registered here once and left unedited (U0a plan step 1).",
    "forge-write-coverage.js declaredFor normalizes each declared write with String(), so an object entry ({root_id, path}) is observed as '[object Object]'; an observation-only limitation that predates issue 343 (the old reader produced 'root_id: primary') and is left unedited."
